  {
   "id": 28,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    -1020,
    0
   ],
   "size": [
    460,
    560
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 27,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "# 4 - Masked character replacement (zero offset)\n\n**Models** (official Comfy-Org files; the loaders carry their download links): ref2va, Qwen3-VL, video + audio VAE.\n\n**Checkpoint variants**: the bf16 checkpoints work in the same loaders (pick them in the list); the Turbo LoRA (4-step ref2v / 8-step fl2v) cuts the steps - set the scheduler steps to match.\n\n**Inputs**: the plate video; a mask video of the subject (white = replace; any segmenter, saved as video); <Picture 1> the new character.\n\n**Controls**: Subject Crop mode / crop_scale / head_size_mode; Image + Reference `ref_video_fit = target grid` puts <Video 1> on the output's own token grid (no half-token offset); Source AV Latent keeps the plate's sound and pins every token outside the mask; Subject Uncrop `exact outside mask` keeps every pixel outside the mask bit-exact; Drift QC measures the exterior; Geometry Report lists offsets.\n\n**Output**: the plate with the subject replaced, plate sound, MP4.\n\n**Limits**: the plate length must be 17k+5 frames (124, 141, ... - Source AV Latent refuses others and names the nearest); crop sizes are on the 32 px grid; the identity inside the mask is the model's choice (soft).\n\n**Status**: built in ComfyUI's own front end and validated by the server (only missing model / media files reported). NOT run on H3 weights on the build machine - starting values follow core's H3 templates (res_multistep, simple, 20 steps, guider cfg 1). Guide: workflows/tasks/README.md."
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "# 4 - Masked character replacement (zero offset)\n\n**Models** (official Comfy-Org files; the loaders carry their download links): ref2va, Qwen3-VL, video + audio VAE.\n\n**Checkpoint variants**: the bf16 checkpoints work in the same loaders (pick them in the list); the Turbo LoRA (4-step ref2v / 8-step fl2v) cuts the steps - set the scheduler steps to match.\n\n**Inputs**: the plate video; a mask video of the subject (white = replace; any segmenter, saved as video); <Picture 1> the new character.\n\n**Controls**: Subject Crop mode / crop_scale / head_size_mode; Image + Reference `ref_video_fit = target grid` puts <Video 1> on the output's own token grid (no half-token offset); Source AV Latent keeps the plate's sound and pins every token outside the mask; Subject Uncrop `exact outside mask` keeps every pixel outside the mask bit-exact; Drift QC measures the exterior; Geometry Report lists offsets.\n\n**Output**: the plate with the subject replaced, plate sound, MP4.\n\n**Limits**: the plate length must be 17k+5 frames (124, 141, ... - Source AV Latent refuses others and names the nearest); crop sizes are on the 32 px grid; the identity inside the mask is the model's choice (soft).\n\n**Status**: built in ComfyUI's own front end and validated by the server (only missing model / media files reported). NOT run on H3 weights on the build machine - starting values follow core's H3 templates (res_multistep, simple, 20 steps, guider cfg 1). Guide: workflows/tasks/README.md."
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
 ],
